{com}. *AIC/BIC for zero inflated  negative binomial are smallest ; hence zero inflated negative binomial model is best for this analysis; 
. 
. *BEFORE VARIABLE SELECTION WE ASSESS IF BP IS KEPT AS CONTINOUS OR CATEGORICAL AND THEN BMI
. 
. *BP
. *BLOOD PRESSURE
. *1.sbp as is
. *2.dbp as is
. *3.binary sbp (high sbp; 140mg and above); yes(1)/no(0)
. *4.binary dbp (high dpb; 100mh and above); yes(1)/no(0)
. *5.hypertension(systolic 140mmHg and above OR diastolic 100mmHg and above); 1(yes) and 0(no)
. 
. *3 binary sbp
. gen high_sbp = 0
{txt}
{com}. replace high_sbp = 1 if sbp >= 140
{txt}(1,470 real changes made)

{com}. replace high_sbp = . if sbp == .
{txt}(0 real changes made)

{com}. label variable high_sbp "High Systolic BP 140+ (1=Yes, 0=No)"
{txt}
{com}. label define yesnolabel 0"No" 1"Yes"
{txt}
{com}. label values high_sbp yesnolabel
{txt}
{com}. 
. *4. binary dbp
. gen high_dbp = 0
{txt}
{com}. replace high_dbp =1 if dbp >= 100
{txt}(476 real changes made)

{com}. replace high_dbp = . if dbp == .
{txt}(0 real changes made)

{com}. label variable high_dbp "High Diastolic BP 100+ (1=Yes, 0=No)"
{txt}
{com}. label values high_dbp yesnolabel
{txt}
{com}. 
. *5 hypertension
. gen hypertension = 0
{txt}
{com}. replace hypertension =1 if sbp >= 140 | dbp >= 100
{txt}(1,492 real changes made)

{com}. replace hypertension = . if sbp ==. & dbp == .
{txt}(0 real changes made)

{com}. label variable hypertension "Hypertension"
{txt}
{com}. label values hypertension yesnolabel
{txt}
{com}. 
. *check
. tab high_sbp 

